WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.409 --> 00:00:05.420
Change Lives.

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:07.220
Change Organizations.

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:11.000
Change the World.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:17.750
When we say change lives, change organizations
and change the world, we really mean it.

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:21.670
Stanford GSB equips students to do that.

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:24.199
You first have to start by changing yourself.

00:00:24.199 --> 00:00:26.670
Students are naturally encouraged to innovate.

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:29.380
Broadens your perspectives on how to influence,
how to lead.

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:31.420
I learned to be a critical, analytical thinker.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:33.890
I understand the global context of management.

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:36.760
At the GSB, I can use virtually the whole
world

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:39.830
while studying at this place. I have access
to

00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:41.890
a lot of leaders of international organizations.

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:46.809
People who start their own companies, film
directors, bankers and private equity consultants.

00:00:46.809 --> 00:00:49.910
Renowned leaders from around the world…Nobel
prize winners.

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:52.160
It’s really a transformational experience.

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:53.160
Change lives.

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:54.250
Change organizations.

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:55.250
Change the world.

00:00:55.250 --> 00:01:00.890
I just came back from the Stanford Tsinghua
exchange program. Austria, Switzerland, Kenya,

00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:01.890
Rwanda.

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:05.950
When the faculty come on these trips we can
bring that experience directly into the classroom.

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:09.500
It’s been inspiring, complicated, exciting.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:11.520
We meet with head of marketing at Red Bull.
We’re meeting with Bay and Capital.

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:19.150
We’re meeting with Shanda. The best company
in China.

00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:21.380
President Kagame, the president of Rwanda;
Daniel arap Moi, the former president of Kenya.

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:22.380
The minister of industry and commerce,

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:25.160
and lessons learned from GSB alums were amazing.

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:29.360
Some alumni are very warm hearted to give
us great career advice.

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:35.530
We have a group of alumni who have had an
incredible impact on the world,

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:37.649
individuals who have lived our mantra.

00:01:37.649 --> 00:01:39.510
Change lives. Change organizations. And Change
the world.

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:40.510
Hoping to change all three.

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:41.510
I’m really interested in entrepreneurship
and innovation. Energy, clean tech space.

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:49.929
We’re working in tourism in Peru, private
equity, combining business and medicine.

00:01:49.929 --> 00:01:55.739
Stanford GSB believes in the individual’s
ability to affect change.

00:01:55.739 --> 00:01:59.629
Make a difference in the lives of, you know,
hundreds, millions of peoples.

00:01:59.629 --> 00:02:00.970
Pursue your dream.

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:02.739
Dream on a world scale.

00:02:02.739 --> 00:02:03.739
Change lives.

00:02:03.739 --> 00:02:05.160
Change organizations.

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:06.170
And change the world.

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:06.180
&gt;&gt;upbeat music

